## Active publication identity

P15 is the **Scientific Execution Integrity (SEI)** systems paper for the ORION research harness and ORION-Q dual harness.

Parent programme: #977.  
Promotion protocol: `papers/paper-15-orion-research-harness/TOP_TIER_PROMOTION_V1.md` on PR #978.

## Maximum claim to earn

> Execution provenance can establish attribution and replay properties without thereby establishing scientific validity. A fail-closed research harness should make this separation explicit: host/capability failures must never be laundered into scientific evidence, receipts must bind what actually executed, publication must be race-safe and non-coercing, and multi-lane agreement must remain distinct from correctness/validity.

P15 does **not** claim provenance, reproducibility, workflow packaging or proof-of-execution in general. Those are donor layers to absorb/interoperate with.

## Separation ladder

Freeze and test the non-implications:

`ATTRIBUTABLE_EXECUTION`
`!= REPLAYABLE_EXECUTION`
`!= AGREEMENT_BETWEEN_EXECUTIONS`
`!= SCIENTIFICALLY_VALID_RESULT`
`!= AUTHORIZED_SCIENTIFIC_CLAIM`

## Required formal/executable invariants

- [ ] H15.1 host/science separation;
- [ ] H15.2 exact invocation/result binding;
- [ ] H15.3 race-safe publication atomicity after required execution/reap/cleanup phases;
- [ ] H15.4 coverage/receipt completeness does not imply scientific validity;
- [ ] H15.5 dual-lane agreement semantics explicitly separated from correctness.

## Donor/interoperability programme

Compare/interoperate with strong applicable classes:

- structured logs/event sourcing;
- W3C PROV / RO-Crate-style provenance;
- reproducible workflow/pipeline systems;
- content-addressed execution/build systems;
- deterministic replay;
- signed/attested proof-of-execution where feasible;
- multi-run/dual-lane agreement systems.

P15's residual must be the **scientific evidence-admission boundary**, not provenance interchange itself.

## Protected fault-injection programme

Freeze a publication-specific adversarial matrix independent of existing implementation debugging. Include at minimum:

- process/setup failures;
- timeout/signal/termination races;
- EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK readiness races;
- exact-cap/cap+1 output sentinels and truncation;
- nonzero exit with misleading output;
- helper/tool failure reported as success;
- cleanup/unregister omission;
- finalization before reap;
- retry exhaustion/accounting corruption;
- stale/replayed/duplicate invocation receipts;
- occurrence identity collisions;
- coverage/prefix omissions;
- forged work/result deltas;
- invalid scientific content with perfectly complete receipts.

## Primary outcomes

- false scientific-success admission;
- host-failure-as-science admission;
- forged/stale/replay detection;
- output completeness failures;
- publication-race failures;
- correct invalid-content / `CANNOT_CHECK` disposition;
- replay fidelity;
- provenance interchange completeness;
- false rejection and runtime/storage overhead;
- dual-lane agreement false reassurance;
- ability to identify attributable-but-scientifically-invalid results.

## Independent authority

The fault injector and gold execution/scientific disposition must be independent from the candidate harness. Scientific validity comes from a frozen external checker/contract, never receipt completeness alone.

## Done when

- [ ] claim/evidence ledger exists;
- [ ] donor matrix closes after changed-vocabulary saturation;
- [ ] publication protocol is frozen before protected outcomes;
- [ ] broad fault-injection benchmark runs against donor comparators;
- [ ] false scientific-success admission is near zero without unacceptable false rejection;
- [ ] explicit receipt/coverage/agreement != validity counterexamples survive;
- [ ] independent replay/adjudication closes;
- [ ] submission manuscript and reproducibility package bind exact results;
- [ ] `P15_TOP_TIER_SUBMISSION_READY` is emitted only by a separate content-addressed closure receipt, never by the planning protocol.

Current state remains `SCIENTIFIC_OBJECT_NOT_YET_EARNED` until protected SEI results exist.

## Mission

Upgrade ORION-Q from a framework that is unusually strong at epistemic custody, hostile checking, and publication synchronization into a framework that **systematically converts exact frontier evidence into reusable structural theorems**.

This issue is additive. It does **not** weaken or rewrite the frozen Phase-4 nine-step cycle, protected-evaluation custody, Q-series publication sync, or existing paper claim boundaries.

The target pipeline is:

`Q-DISCOVER -> Q-REFEREE -> Q-PUBLISH`.

Current ORION is strongest in the latter two. This issue defines the missing discovery layer.

## Why now

The ORION-RG Davenport programme has produced the exact pattern this layer should exploit:

- exact finite constants (`D_2(C_5^3)=20`, `D_3(C_5^3)=25`);
- large exact classifications (1,405 `D_2` extremal GL classes; 26,369 maximal zero-sum-free GL classes);
- a genuine structural reduction covering 65% of the inverse `C_5^3` census;
- a complete negative theorem closing the threshold/peeling direction;
- repeated cases where a striking computational regularity was later found to be donor mathematics.

The next gain should come from **compression into mechanism**, not from accumulating more unstructured exact data.

## Breakthrough levels

Every flagship-relevant result receives a non-authoritative structural level:

- `B0` — experiment/observation;
- `B1` — exact finite value;
- `B2` — exhaustive classification;
- `B3` — structural lemma explaining a classification or obstruction;
- `B4` — reusable parametric theorem / genuinely new infinite family;
- `B5` — major conjecture resolved/refuted or broadly reusable new mechanism.

This is a prioritization coordinate, **not** a truth or novelty score. Ordinary theorem/proof/novelty authority remains external to it.

Default flagship policy: a top-tier scientific headline should normally target `B4+`; `B1/B2` remain publishable when independently important but should not terminate theorem synthesis automatically.

## D1 — COMPRESSION_GATE

After an exact census/search, the next expensive computation is refused unless it is designed to reduce the dimensionality of the unknown or discriminate a pre-frozen structural hypothesis.

Required sequence:

`raw objects -> candidate signatures -> ablation -> minimal sufficient coordinates -> structural types -> mechanism -> theorem candidate`.

For every proposed coordinate, remove it and ask whether mathematically different continuation/outcome states collapse. Coordinates that are necessary under hostile ablation become theorem-synthesis candidates; coordinates that add no discrimination are dropped.

A bigger atlas is not progress by itself.

## D2 — OBSTRUCTION_TO_INVARIANT

Every failed theorem attempt must terminate in at least one of:

1. a replayable counterexample;
2. a minimal obstruction;
3. a newly required state coordinate;
4. a proved impossibility result closing the method family;
5. `CANNOT_CHECK` with the exact resource/evidence boundary.

No generic `did not work` terminal.

Do not widen `1-swap -> 2-swap -> global search` merely because a search failed. First identify the invariant trapping the smaller grammar. The invariant, not the larger search, is the preferred successor object.

## D3 — two-sided theorem laboratory

For every B3+ conjecture freeze two logically isolated attack packets before protected outcomes:

- **proof packet** — strongest symbolic route to the conjecture;
- **counterexample packet** — construct the hardest world satisfying all premises while falsifying the conclusion.

A synthesis packet may be opened only after both packets are sealed. It asks which premise the proof needs that the counterexample programme cannot realize. That intersection is a first-class missing-lemma candidate.

Agreement between packets is not correctness authority.

## D4 — SYMBOLIC_LIFT

Every finite theorem/certificate at B2/B3 immediately undergoes a symbolic lift before publication framing is frozen.

Replace load-bearing constants by parameters and record:

- which proof steps are genuinely constant-specific;
- which depend only on rank/exponent/primary decomposition/etc.;
- the second parameter point/family on which the same mechanism should work;
- the first predicted failure boundary;
- donor theorems that already own any lifted form.

A finite result may remain the paper if it is independently important, but generalization is tested before ORION declares the scientific ceiling.

## D5 — HARD_STRATUM

When a theorem handles a strict subset of an exact census, freeze the complement as a named hard stratum and stop recomputing the solved region.

For each hard stratum record:

- defining invariant boundary;
- size/orbit count;
- exact reason the solved proof fails;
- smallest additional state coordinate that could repair the proof;
- candidate reductions to lower-rank / donor-owned objects.

This is intended to turn failures of induction/normalization into structured theorem targets.

## D6 — breakthrough portfolio

Maintain three live flagship roles, not an unlimited queue:

- `A_EXPLOIT` — strongest tractable theorem path;
- `B_STRUCTURE` — deeper structural compression problem;
- `C_BOUNDARY` — high-risk counterexample/general-conjecture attack.

Score only for scheduling, never truth:

`impact * novelty-confidence * generalization-leverage * tractability`.

A lane killed by donor literature, impossibility theorem, or exact obstruction is reallocated rather than rhetorically rescued.

## D7 — compute-to-compress rule

Before material new compute, state which one of these it is expected to do:

- distinguish two theorem hypotheses;
- expose a minimal obstruction;
- test a symbolic lift on a new family;
- classify a hard stratum under a frozen signature;
- independently replay/refute a claimed certificate.

If none applies, the computation is presumptively low priority.

## D8 — publication coupling

The existing Q-series top-tier refactor remains authoritative for current papers. This layer changes **future research selection**, not historical claims.

Publication packets should report breakthrough level and compression history as internal provenance only. Manuscripts should state the native theorem/mechanism, not ORION process terminology, unless the framework itself is the study object.

## First live calibration — ORION-RG

Use the current rank-3 Davenport programme as the first prospective calibration:

- `A_EXPLOIT`: one-block/affine-deficit repair for `C_45^3` and symbolic primary-power lift;
- `B_STRUCTURE`: the unresolved maximal-zero-sum-free `C_5^3` hard stratum after the multiplicity-4 quotient theorem;
- `C_BOUNDARY`: exact/structural multiwise gate around `D_4(C_5^3)` and its effect on general `C_n^3` induction.

The calibration is successful only if the new layer changes a research decision or produces a smaller theorem-bearing state. It is not validated because the vocabulary looks plausible.

## Hostile controls

- rediscovered theorem is donor absorption, not B4 novelty;
- exhaustive finite coverage does not self-promote to an infinite theorem;
- compression score cannot replace semantic sufficiency proof;
- a selected invariant that only correlates with outcomes is B0/B1 evidence;
- failed symbolic lift must be preserved as a boundary result;
- publication prestige is not a truth signal;
- framework scoring cannot grant mathematical authority;
- no modification of protected Task-3 branch/files or frozen cycle semantics from this issue.

## Deliverables

- additive `BREAKTHROUGH_ENGINE_PROTOCOL_V1.md`;
- machine-readable breakthrough-level / portfolio schema only if it adds testable value;
- at least one prospective RG cycle using COMPRESSION_GATE and SYMBOLIC_LIFT;
- one proof-vs-counterexample synthesis packet;
- one hard-stratum ablation report;
- one publication decision where B-level/generalization evidence materially changes the target;
- claim ledger initialized without breakthrough/novelty authority.

## Strong terminals

- `ORION_Q_DISCOVERY_LAYER_PROSPECTIVELY_USEFUL`;
- `ORION_Q_DISCOVERY_LAYER_NARROWED`;
- `ORION_Q_DISCOVERY_LAYER_NO_INCREMENTAL_VALUE`;
- `ORION_Q_DISCOVERY_LAYER_REDISCOVERS_DONOR_ONLY`;
- `ORION_Q_DISCOVERY_LAYER_CANNOT_CHECK`.

## Claim boundary

This issue does **not** claim that ORION causes breakthroughs. The scientific claim, if any, must be earned prospectively against real frontier decisions and ordinary expert/mathematical authority. The immediate purpose is operational: make theorem-level compression and generalization the default research objective rather than an optional afterthought.

